    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46458" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suf-frīgĭdus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subf-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>rather cold</i> or <i>frigid</i>
			(post-class. and very rare); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trop.: argumentum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 17, 11, 4</span></i>
			. —<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suffrīgĭdē</span></b> , <i>rather coldly</i> or <i>frigidly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nimis minute ac prope etiam suffrigide,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					2, 9, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
